    Bump query-string from 9.5.1 to 10.0.0 in /modules/lti (#8201)
    
    Bumps [query-string](https://github.com/sindresorhus/query-string) from
    9.5.1 to 10.0.0.
    <details>
    <summary>Release notes</summary>
    <p><em>Sourced from <a
    href="https://github.com/sindresorhus/query-string/releases">query-string's
    releases</a>.</em></p>
    <blockquote>
    <h2>v10.0.0</h2>
    <h3>Breaking</h3>
    <ul>
    <li>Require Node.js 22  dc9cd5e</li>
    <li><code>stringify()</code> now throws a <code>TypeError</code> for
    values it cannot represent, like objects, functions, symbols, and
    <code>Date</code> 99d9c07
    <ul>
    <li>Before, <code>{a: {}}</code> became
    <code>a=%5Bobject%20Object%5D</code>. Use the <a
    href="https://github.com/sindresorhus/query-string?tab=readme-ov-file#replacer"><code>replacer</code></a>
    option to convert such values.</li>
    </ul>
    </li>
    <li><code>parse()</code> now collects a repeated key into an array with
    every <a
    href="https://github.com/sindresorhus/query-string?tab=readme-ov-file#arrayformat"><code>arrayFormat</code></a>
    27018f4 a6d6a7f
    <ul>
    <li>Before, <code>bracket</code>, <code>index</code>,
    <code>colon-list-separator</code>, <code>bracket-separator</code>,
    <code>comma</code>, and <code>separator</code> kept only the last value,
    so <code>foo=1&amp;foo=2</code> gave <code>{foo: '2'}</code>.</li>
    </ul>
    </li>
    <li>An explicit <a
    href="https://github.com/sindresorhus/query-string?tab=readme-ov-file#types"><code>types</code></a>
    entry now always takes precedence over <code>parseNumbers</code> and
    <code>parseBooleans</code>, and a value that does not match its type
    stays a string 04649de f48a249</li>
    <li>The <code>string[]</code> and <code>number[]</code> types now always
    give an array (except with <code>arrayFormat: 'none'</code>, as
    documented) 04649de 2a6984f</li>
    <li>A percent-encoded byte that is not valid UTF-8 now decodes to
    <code>U+FFFD</code>, like <code>URLSearchParams</code>, instead of being
    kept as-is 19331de</li>
    <li><code>arrayFormat: 'bracket-separator'</code> no longer splits on a
    percent-encoded separator, like <code>comma</code> and
    <code>separator</code> (<a
    href="https://redirect.github.com/sindresorhus/query-string/issues/398">#398</a>)
    deb9784
    <ul>
    <li><code>foo[]=a%2Cb,c</code> now gives <code>['a,b', 'c']</code>.</li>
    </ul>
    </li>
    <li><code>stringifyUrl()</code> now percent-encodes <code>%</code> in
    <code>fragmentIdentifier</code> 1602ae0
    <ul>
    <li>The fragment identifier is now a decoded value, like the query
    values, so it round-trips with <code>parseUrl()</code>. If you passed an
    already encoded fragment identifier, pass it decoded.</li>
    </ul>
    </li>
    <li><code>pick()</code> and <code>exclude()</code> now write the kept
    parameters back exactly as they were in the URL 1646c64 e087ca9 a7391f2
    <ul>
    <li>Options like <code>parseNumbers</code>, <code>parseBooleans</code>,
    <code>types</code>, and <code>decode</code> only change the value the
    filter receives. Before, <code>pick('https://foo.bar?id=007', ['id'],
    {parseNumbers: true})</code> gave <code>id=7</code>.</li>
    </ul>
    </li>
    </ul>
    <h3>Improvements</h3>
    <ul>
    <li>Remove the <code>decode-uri-component</code> dependency and decode
    in linear time 19331de
    <ul>
    <li>The old decoder was quadratic for some malformed input.</li>
    </ul>
    </li>
    <li>Fix <code>parse()</code> being quadratic for a key that repeats many
    times with <code>arrayFormat: 'comma'</code> and
    <code>'separator'</code> 00a52ff</li>
    <li>TypeScript: The parsed value types now follow the
    <code>parseNumbers</code>, <code>parseBooleans</code>, and
    <code>types</code> options, also for <code>parseUrl()</code>,
    <code>pick()</code>, and <code>exclude()</code> d239f4f 472777f
    789fc36</li>
    <li>An option that is explicitly <code>undefined</code> now uses its
    default value 1646c64</li>
    </ul>
    <h3>Fixes</h3>
    <ul>
    <li>Fix <code>stringify()</code> output that did not parse back to the
    same value 13bc381 b63dc56 deb9784
    <ul>
    <li>This affected a separator like <code>-</code> or <code>.</code>
    inside a value, <code>null</code> items with
    <code>colon-list-separator</code>, and arrays that became empty after
    skipping items with <code>bracket-separator</code>.</li>
    </ul>
    </li>
    <li>Fix <code>stringify()</code> throwing <code>URIError</code> for a
    string with a lone surrogate b9ff3f8</li>
    <li>Fix the <code>sort</code> option  220906a 678ddff 6c6506d
    <ul>
    <li><code>sort: true</code> threw in <code>stringify()</code>,
    <code>parse()</code> threw when <code>sort</code> was not a boolean or a
    function, <code>sort: false</code> broke <code>arrayFormat:
    'index'</code>, and <code>pick()</code> ignored <code>sort:
    false</code>.</li>
    </ul>
    </li>
    <li>Fix <code>stringifyUrl()</code> turning an <code>index</code> format
    array that is already in the URL into <code>[object Object]</code> (<a
    href="https://redirect.github.com/sindresorhus/query-string/issues/422">#422</a>)
    220906a</li>
    <li>Fix <code>stringifyUrl()</code>, <code>pick()</code>, and
    <code>exclude()</code> corrupting the query and the fragment identifier
    with <code>encode: false</code> 7268b7a c75c681</li>
    <li>Fix <code>stringifyUrl()</code> changing the parameters that are
    already in the URL when you give it parse options 93c3e1e</li>
    <li>Fix <code>parseUrl()</code> and <code>stringifyUrl()</code> keeping
    leading and trailing whitespace 1d91dbf 93c3e1e</li>
    <li>Fix <code>parse()</code> throwing for <code>arrayFormat:
    'index'</code> when a plain value comes before the indexed entries
    8e9d58d</li>
    <li>Fix <code>parse()</code> using <code>types</code> keys inherited
    from <code>Object.prototype</code>, like <code>toString</code> (<a
    href="https://redirect.github.com/sindresorhus/query-string/issues/421">#421</a>)
    0682872</li>
    <li>Fix <code>stringify()</code> ignoring the <code>replacer</code>
    result for <code>skipNull</code> and <code>skipEmptyString</code>
    42210ea</li>
    <li>Fix <code>stringify()</code> reading each value twice, which ran
    getters and <code>Proxy</code> traps two times 5e50210</li>
    <li>Fix <code>stringifyUrl()</code> not accepting an
    <code>interface</code> for <code>query</code> cd042b8</li>
    </ul>
